# Next.js + Tailwind CSS v4 Rules

## Tailwind v4 CSS Writing Rules (most important)

### Custom CSS in `globals.css` must always be written inside `@layer base`.

Tailwind v4 uses CSS Cascade Layers.
CSS written outside a layer will **always override** Tailwind utility classes, regardless of specificity.
(This disables all spacing classes such as `px-*`, `py-*`, `gap-*`, `m-*`, `h-*`.)

```css
/* ❌ BAD — a `*` reset outside a layer overrides every Tailwind spacing utility */
@import 'tailwindcss';

* {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* ✅ GOOD — put it inside @layer base so Tailwind utilities work correctly */
@import 'tailwindcss';

@layer base {
  * {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  body {
    font-family: 'Pretendard', sans-serif;
  }
}
```

### Tailwind v4 import syntax

```css
/* ❌ BAD (v3 syntax) */
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

/* ✅ GOOD (v4 syntax) */
@import 'tailwindcss';
```

